Derivation
----------

ZEN began as a fork of niri, and this notice exists to satisfy GPL-3.0 section 5:
the original copyright is preserved, and the modifications are stated.

    niri
    Copyright (C) Ivan Molodetskikh <yalterz@gmail.com> and contributors
    https://github.com/niri-wm/niri
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.

ZEN branched from niri at version 26.4.0 and has been modified extensively since.
The layout engine was replaced outright: niri's one-dimensional scrollable strip
became an unbounded two-dimensional canvas of free-positioned islands, navigated
by a per-output camera, in which maximize is a viewport operation that sends the
window no configure at all. That camera, the canvas coordinate system, the island
model, the spatial navigation, the glass material and the compositor-drawn canvas
widgets are ZEN's own work.

Substantial parts of the surrounding compositor remain derived from niri: the
Smithay backends, the Wayland protocol implementations, Xwayland integration, the
animation and gesture systems, the GLSL rendering pipeline, the KDL configuration
layer and the IPC. Those parts carry niri's copyright above.

This is a modified version. It is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or supported
by the niri project, and problems with ZEN should not be reported to them.
